ground=dict(source_ids=['reply-queue','reset-append','leader-match','tracker-commit','majority','log-eligibility'],expectation_ids=['durability-expectation','async-contract'],binding_ids=[binding],derivation='The implementation explicitly requires entries to be persisted before being counted toward commitment (durability-expectation). The async contract permits outgoing replication before local writes but requires storage-worker responses after ordered durable completion. Under a fixed simple voting configuration, commitment may use any majority of persisted matching replicas; it does not require the leader itself to have persisted when other replicas form a majority. This requirement is independent of the observed committed value and of a blanket expectation that delayed local writes block every commit.',applicability='Non-Byzantine peers; stable fixed simple voter membership; async storage mode; current-term ordinary proposal; honest ordered storage workers, no crashes or data corruption. MemoryStorage represents successfully completed storage writes at the library boundary; no physical disk durability is measured.',unresolved=[],conflicts=[],alternatives=['A three-voter leader may legally commit using both followers while its own append worker is delayed.'])
